  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are based on a single extreme flooding event in Germany, which may limit how well these specific narrative and emotional trajectories generalize to other disaster types or cultural contexts.",
      "what": "The study analyzed approximately 2,700 Instagram posts spanning a three-year period following the July 2021 extreme flooding in western Germany. Using ChatGPT-4 supervised by humans to classify images into six visual themes, the method achieved an 80.73% agreement rate and a Cohen's kappa of 0.74 compared to manual coding. The analysis mapped how visual themes shifted from immediate damage to long-term recovery, alongside a corresponding emotional transition from anxiety to hope.",
      "why": "It demonstrates that AI-assisted visual classification can reliably scale up the analysis of social media imagery during crises, revealing nuanced emotional and narrative shifts that traditional hashtag-only analyses fail to capture."
